 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "Contract: the synthesized default page (and every Studio-seeded record page, via createSeed) now writes visibleWhen onto an ENUMERATED record:details section, a key @objectstack/spec RecordDetailsProps.sections[] refuses on parse (unrecognized_keys, measured with control). record:details honours it on any section, so a hand-authored sections[].visibleWhen also renders gated while the spec refuses it. How should the contract converge?",
   "options": [
    "A: objectstack declares visibleWhen on the record:details section entry (same EvaluatedExpression input as FormSectionSchema.visibleWhen) and adds it to that surface's derivedKeys, so it is refused beside group and inherited through it; objectui then mirrors it in RecordDetailsComponentProps.sections[] and the registered inputs. Cost: one spec key + mirror; follows the declare-what-the-renderer-honours rulings that declared hideEmpty/collapsible/showBorder/defaultCollapsed/icon/description/headerColor on this same entry.",
    "B: the synthesizer and createSeed emit the spec-legal { group } reference for group-derived sections (the spec already says it inherits visibleWhen), keeping the predicate internal to the renderer's group resolution, and the renderer stops reading visibleWhen off enumerated sections. Cost: app-shell RecordDetailView change (outside this claim), seeded pages start tracking group membership, and a page body then depends on objectSchema being in record context; also retires the pre-existing rich-fields off-spec emission for grouped sections.",
    "C: leave as delivered (undeclared key emitted by our own producer and honoured by the renderer)."
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. Business need is measured (the QA checklist clause, and the form already honours the same predicate). Long-term: it converges on one declared contract with FormSection parity instead of a renderer-only reading. AI-safety: declared = enforced, and the AI-facing trap of C (renderer honours what the spec refuses) closes. Startup scope: it adds one key that already has a live producer and consumer, no new capability. B is the stricter no-new-key route but is larger and moves a seed shape; C leaves the drift."
  },
  {
   "question": "Fault direction: @objectstack/spec's deriveFieldGroupLayout TSDoc says section gating is the renderer's contract with FALSE hiding the group 'fail-closed', while objectui's form (pinned by section-grouping-6236 FAULTED leg) and now the detail page fail OPEN on a predicate that cannot be evaluated. This PR follows the form per the card's ruling; which side should move?",
   "options": [
    "A: keep fail-open on both surfaces (ADR-0137 D3 render direction) and correct the spec TSDoc wording.",
    "B: flip both surfaces to fail-closed for SECTION predicates (a shipped-behaviour change for the form, needs its own ruling)."
   ],
   "recommendation": "No recommendation from this seat beyond keeping the two surfaces on one shared evaluator so either answer moves both; A is the smaller change, B matches the spec prose."
  }
 ],
 "out_of_scope_findings": [
  "class: b · reach: named producer — Studio page-create createSeed (app-shell metadata-admin anchors.ts) stores buildDefaultPageSchema(objectDef).regions as a page row · evidence: for an object with fieldGroups, RecordDetailsProps.safeParse(buildDefaultDetails(def).properties) on installed spec 17.6.0 returns invalid_type at every sections.N.fields.M, because deriveFieldGroupDetailSections emits rich field descriptors where the spec declares z.array(z.string()); buildDefaultPageSchema.strictPayload.test.ts judges nodes with PageComponentSchema, which leaves properties unjudged, so no pin sees it · Seam: spec:RecordDetailsProps.sections[].fields → runtime:createSeed (Studio page create) | renderer:record:details · dedupe words: record:details sections fields rich descriptors; createSeed buildDefaultPageSchema RecordDetailsProps; synthesized page properties unjudged; strictPayload PageComponentSchema properties",
